      "message": "Good observation but given how central `match` is to Rust, I would be horrified to see the compiler generate a long string of `if-elif-elif-elif-...`.\n\nIn fact, what this compiles to (almost) exactly what you suggested:\n```\n000000007fc13d70 \u003cstrerror\u003e:\n    7fc13d70:   7102141f        cmp     w0, #0x85\n    7fc13d74:   540000c8        b.hi    7fc13d8c \u003cstrerror+0x1c\u003e  // b.pmore\n    7fc13d78:   d503201f        nop\n    7fc13d7c:   10150a88        adr     x8, 7fc3decc \u003canon.44ec2ef2190491864f9217973fa8ea4c.163.llvm.976358234094013073+0x36\u003e\n    7fc13d80:   b8a05909        ldrsw   x9, [x8, w0, uxtw #2]\n    7fc13d84:   8b090100        add     x0, x8, x9\n    7fc13d88:   d65f03c0        ret\n    7fc13d8c:   d503201f        nop\n    7fc13d90:   1014ac40        adr     x0, 7fc3d318 \u003cstderr+0x8\u003e\n    7fc13d94:   d65f03c0        ret\n```",
